#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059490 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "7bfcfcbb-6212-5f9b-90aa-c79fbf7221e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-4518" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/ed434344208758284aa0f144676f7dd6498a63faeb0248d18e87c4be6c3d87f2.png)\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y+0z=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/b9364923447e278db5ec47bef74e1a05310645b30df22d4ea5efcc0de46c6ed2.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/16cb1608f70821d138f0c6984038bb42d86d9fbf76d560d94d2e25bd6fdb05e0.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/0abbbaf34955fa40d6cdbfa9e16cb1567ee16271d65b4565206a0f2204eedf6d.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/4b915439c3e9922d692aab4205a728160e0a1286f82fa5ebc736460901581147.png)\n\nTherefore, $a=6,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059491 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/id #uuid "c4af8b0d-e4ee-56f4-9cf6-594530639339" :question/math-academy-id "e-4519" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ z-x+2=-1 \\\\ 2y-2x-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/0d06481c63a618262b9034124c24cd1d0c566ee9d6b891fa470e09dc67f5f6c6.png)\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ -x+0y+z=-3 \\\\ -2x+2y-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/104c591a6a72cf3caab1bc2a965c57258bb37a31578254696e0c1cd740fe5915.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/e008383384401198e67f648cce33a720d98afb6a6f60a14ba7ffa21dcc095a5f.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/c85e33202a691b685431ac16efab6a7fd932eac056743df6e81632587f0465b2.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/64d1f57717dda57c8a7fbc403728ee9699a22ce995f68a50a0b80f25543fdab6.png)\n\nTherefore $a=0,$ $b=-2,$ $c=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330329 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea142ec8-5dd7-5a9b-9e06-dcdb6db57742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=5,\\,c=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330331} {:answer/id #uuid "25e57de6-3fc4-5fa7-af00-5f628060c8a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=4,\\,b=1,\\,c=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330332} {:answer/id #uuid "df0ca58e-cc2e-51e6-91ce-63f4ad40ee6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-7,\\,b=1,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330333} {:answer/id #uuid "1df6607c-5133-5d94-85c7-8a04d4fab857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330334} {:answer/id #uuid "02238340-e005-5423-8044-8e5905140f02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=-7,\\,c=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1df6607c-5133-5d94-85c7-8a04d4fab857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330334} :answer-field/id #uuid "247f7b3a-42e3-5c20-a1dc-8036e2c18eba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f48fae54-75c1-5735-95b2-656baa979098" :question/math-academy-id "q-130562" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}z-7x-5=0 \\\\ 4y-x-3z-2=0 \\\\ 2y+x-8=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & a \\\\ b & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-7x+0y+z=5 \\\\ -x+4y-3z=2 \\\\ x+2y+0z=6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330367 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "614d19c8-9998-5a5e-b557-ba50f566abcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-2,\\,b=-1,\\,c=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330369} {:answer/id #uuid "18f9f8f7-0fbb-50f8-8960-e3feefaeaf20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-2,\\,b=-4,\\,c=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330370} {:answer/id #uuid "1edcddf3-971a-5fa8-a22d-9e57a1a2245f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=5,\\,b=4,\\,c=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330371} {:answer/id #uuid "49414cb7-7641-5475-8b14-0104ac5e4734" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-5,\\,b=-4,\\,c=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330372} {:answer/id #uuid "88ba2c9a-e82c-503e-9b2c-eac9f24df940" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-5,\\,b=-1,\\,c=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18f9f8f7-0fbb-50f8-8960-e3feefaeaf20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-2,\\,b=-4,\\,c=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330370} :answer-field/id #uuid "af2b5a8d-a99b-594c-a3fb-95853ef62c2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a147cf2-1edd-5a7f-9f80-a95a1f3975b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-75512" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-2z+x-5y=1 \\\\ -y+5z-4x=-2 \\\\ 2x-6y-z=2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & a \\\\ b & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & c & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x-5y-2z=1 \\\\ -4x-y+5z=-2 \\\\ 2x-6y-z=2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-2,\\,b=-4,\\,c=-6.$"}]}
